1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,832
Meet Aqua Advisory: sugarcane irrigation intelligence.

2
00:00:02,832 --> 00:00:09,450
This prototype brings farm data, soil moisture prediction, and water balance planning
into one practical dashboard.

3
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:11,911
Start with the overview.

4
00:00:11,911 --> 00:00:15,814
The loaded dataset contains one thousand farms across ten villages.

5
00:00:15,814 --> 00:00:20,888
Summary cards show near-term irrigation needs, estimated water demand, and area under
advisory.

6
00:00:20,888 --> 00:00:25,962
The three-dimensional fleet view and priority list help identify farms needing
attention first.

7
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:30,070
Open a farm advisory and select a plot.

8
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:33,811
Set the planting date, soil texture, irrigation method, and pump flow.

9
00:00:33,811 --> 00:00:36,531
Here we switch from furrow to drip irrigation.

10
00:00:36,531 --> 00:00:40,612
Optional probe readings and rainfall inputs let the plan reflect field conditions.

11
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:47,586
The advisory combines a soil moisture estimate with the F A O fifty-six water
balance.

12
00:00:47,586 --> 00:00:52,822
It shows the next irrigation date, estimated pump duration, crop water use, and
stress status.

13
00:00:52,822 --> 00:00:58,756
The water balance chart then projects depletion over fourteen days, making the
irrigation trigger and assumptions visible.

14
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:05,110
The crop and soil view connects the recommendation to the root zone.

15
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:08,244
Rotate the soil profile to see available water and the

16
00:01:08,244 --> 00:01:11,378
irrigation threshold, alongside crop stage and the crop coefficient curve.

17
00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:16,926
Next, test a scenario without changing the farm record.

18
00:01:16,926 --> 00:01:19,708
Adjust an input, then run the simulator.

19
00:01:19,708 --> 00:01:25,271
The comparison shows how predicted moisture, irrigation timing, water volume, and
pump hours respond.

20
00:01:25,271 --> 00:01:28,450
These are model-based comparisons, not measured field outcomes.

21
00:01:29,350 --> 00:01:32,711
The fleet map brings farm priorities into a spatial view.

22
00:01:32,711 --> 00:01:35,736
Filter by village or irrigation status, inspect plot boundaries,

23
00:01:35,736 --> 00:01:39,097
and switch between two-dimensional mapping and the three-dimensional fleet display.

24
00:01:39,097 --> 00:01:41,450
Individual farms remain accessible from the fleet.

25
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:45,807
Fleet analytics turns individual plans into a wider demand picture.

26
00:01:45,807 --> 00:01:50,993
Compare villages, inspect the fourteen-day demand calendar, and review estimated
water volumes and pump hours.

27
00:01:50,993 --> 00:01:54,450
The village summary can also be exported for further planning.

28
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:57,830
Pump scheduling translates demand into operating slots.

29
00:01:57,830 --> 00:02:02,435
Choose a village, a planning horizon, and the maximum number of simultaneous pumps.

30
00:02:02,435 --> 00:02:07,749
Build the schedule to see feeder load and farm assignments within the configured
supply windows.

31
00:02:07,749 --> 00:02:11,646
Unmet hours remain visible when the available capacity cannot cover demand.

32
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:17,236
The interface supports English, Kannada, Hindi, and Marathi.

33
00:02:17,236 --> 00:02:20,121
Switching language updates the dashboard and advisory text.

34
00:02:20,121 --> 00:02:24,450
Read-aloud and export controls make the recommendation easier to communicate and
review.

35
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:30,050
Model Insights separates a strong random holdout score from performance on unseen
locations.

36
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:32,942
The report compares random, village, and taluk validation.

37
00:02:32,942 --> 00:02:36,196
Geographic generalization is a limitation here, so the displayed

38
00:02:36,196 --> 00:02:39,450
results should guide further data collection and field validation.

39
00:02:40,350 --> 00:02:43,472
The review form lets a field officer, agronomist, or

40
00:02:43,472 --> 00:02:46,941
farmer accept, modify, or reject an advisory and add comments.

41
00:02:46,941 --> 00:02:49,369
This keeps human judgment in the workflow.

42
00:02:49,369 --> 00:02:51,450
No demonstration review is submitted here.

43
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:54,835
Aqua Advisory connects prediction, planning, and review.

44
00:02:54,835 --> 00:02:59,450
A transparent prototype for irrigation decisions, with every recommendation subject
to field confirmation.
